Real-Time Fraud Detection & Risk Analytics System is a machine learning-based application designed to identify potentially fraudulent financial transactions and assign a corresponding risk level. The system analyzes transaction characteristics such as transaction amount, transaction time, device type, location changes, failed attempts, transaction frequency, account age, and distance from the previous transaction.

The project implements a complete machine learning pipeline, starting from transaction data generation and preprocessing, followed by feature engineering, model training, evaluation, and real-time prediction. A Random Forest Classifier is used to classify transactions based on their fraud risk.

The trained model is integrated with a Streamlit dashboard, allowing users to enter transaction details and instantly receive a fraud probability, risk score, and risk level.

🚀 Key Features
📊 Synthetic financial transaction dataset generation
🧹 Data cleaning and preprocessing
⚙️ Feature engineering for fraud-related patterns
🤖 Random Forest-based fraud classification
📈 Model evaluation using accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score and ROC-AUC
🔢 Real-time fraud probability prediction
🎯 Dynamic risk scoring from 0–100
🚦 Risk classification into Low, Medium, and High
🖥️ Interactive Streamlit dashboard
🌐 FastAPI backend for prediction APIs
💾 Saved ML model and preprocessing components using Pickle
📓 Exploratory analysis through Jupyter Notebook
